### Auth API test requests
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Click "Send Request" above each ### block. Run the dev server first: npm run dev
###
### The access token is returned in the response body, not a cookie. Capture it from a
### register/login/refresh response and paste it into @accessToken below, then re-send.
### The extension keeps cookies automatically within this file for the refresh_token cookie.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@accessToken = REPLACE_ME

### 1. Register a member
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "confirmPassword": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Test User",
  "phone": "9812345678"
}

### 2. Register an agency - missing agencyName/licenseNumber, expect 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agency@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "confirmPassword": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Himalayan Homes",
  "phone": "9812345679",
  "type": "agency"
}

### 3. Register an agency - complete body, expect verificationStatus "PENDING"
# @name registerAgency
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agency@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "confirmPassword": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Himalayan Homes",
  "phone": "9812345679",
  "type": "agency",
  "agencyName": "Himalayan Homes Pvt. Ltd.",
  "licenseNumber": "NB-LIC-0001"
}

### 4. Register again with the same email - expect 409 CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "confirmPassword": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Test User",
  "phone": "9812345678"
}

### 5. Register with a role field in the body - should still come back as "role": "USER"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "confirmPassword": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Sneaky User",
  "phone": "9812345680",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "isAdmin": true
}

### 6. Login as the user from step 1 - copy accessToken from the response into @accessToken above
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

### 7. Login with the wrong password - expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "totally-wrong-password"
}

### 8. Login with an email that doesn't exist - expect the SAME 401 message as step 7
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-here@example.com",
  "password": "whatever-password"
}

### 9. Missing Content-Type header - expect 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

### 10. Who am I? (paste the accessToken from step 6 into @accessToken first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 11. Refresh the access token (rotates the refresh token cookie too)
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

### 12. Confirm /me still works with the newly refreshed accessToken
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13. Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

### 14. Refresh after logout should be 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

###
### --- Password reset ---

### 15. Request a reset link - always 204, check the server console for the logged link
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

### 16. Reset the password using the token logged to the console
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_SERVER_CONSOLE",
  "password": "a-brand-new-password"
}

###
### --- Admin ---
### Use the ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD you put in .env when you ran `npm run db:seed`.
### There is no separate admin login endpoint - same /auth/login as everyone else.

### 17. Login as admin (fill in your real admin email/password first)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "your-admin-password"
}

### 18. Approve the agency registered in step 3 (paste the admin accessToken and the agency user id)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/PASTE_AGENCY_USER_ID/verification
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "APPROVED"
}
